  "term": "repeated acquisition",
  "definition": "Repeated acquisition means that the same trait evolved more than once in separate evolutionary lineages, rather than being inherited from a single common origin. In this source, it refers to different early synapsid groups independently developing a three-vertebra sacrum.",
